# aihaus-okf engine

This project uses the **aihaus-okf** engine. The whole system — memory, workflows, agents,
skills — lives in **`.aihaus-okf/`**. This rule is just the door.

## First move, every task
1. Read **`.aihaus-okf/routing.md`** (the Map) and **`.aihaus-okf/conventions.md`** (naming).
2. Use the routing table to load **only** the room the task needs. Do not read everything.

## Quick map
- Work board → `.aihaus-okf/memory/kanban/` (tasks; status = folder)
- Project brain → `.aihaus-okf/memory/project/` (durable markdown facts/rules/decisions)
- Code index → `.aihaus-okf/memory/codebase/` (rebuildable vec over code; see its README)
- Processes → `.aihaus-okf/workflows/` · Roles → `.aihaus-okf/agents/` · How-tos → `.aihaus-okf/skills/`

## Rules
- All project-specific files live under `.aihaus-okf/memory/`.
- Markdown is the source of truth; the code index is a cache — rebuild it with the
  `map-codebase` skill, never trust it over the actual code.
- Write to `memory/project/` deliberately via the `promote-memory` skill.
- Keep this rule short. Detail belongs in the room it concerns.
